 "intro_html": "The creamy white one, modelled on Momofuku’s ramen. The broth starts as a pot of <a href=\"shiitake-kombu-dashi.html\">kombu–shiitake dashi</a>, then runs through <b>three bone stages in the same pot</b>: chicken with onion, then pork with ginger and garlic, then beef — 6–8 hours each, lifting every batch out with a spider before the next goes in: bring each stage up on medium heat, then let it go low for the hours. Chashu is pork belly rolled up skin side out, tied, marinated ~12 hours and roasted hot then low; a whole soy-seared octopus tentacle goes on top.",
