 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Start with a big pot of <a href=\"shiitake-kombu-dashi.html\">kombu–shiitake dashi</a> — about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"l\" data-a=\"6\" data-s=\"0\">6 litres</span>, in the stockpot the broth will cook in.</li><li>Everything after this cooks in that same liquid.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Make the dashi",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/ramen/1.webp",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": "Broth",
   "part_id": "part-broth",
   "time": "~1 h",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 h</span>",
   "title": "Make the dashi",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"l\" data-a=\"6\">6 l</span> — <a href=\"shiitake-kombu-dashi.html\">see recipe</a>",
     "name_html": "Kombu-shiitake dashi"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Put all the bones in a pot, cover with cold water, bring to a boil and boil hard for 10–15 minutes.</li><li>Lots of grey scum comes up — that’s the point.</li><li>Drain everything into the sink.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "high",
    "label_html": "<span>high</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Blanch the bones",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Cover all the bones with cold water, then bring it to a hard boil.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/2-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/2.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": "Broth",
   "part_id": "part-broth",
   "time": "10–15 min",
   "time_html": "<span>10–15 min</span>",
   "title": "Blanch the bones",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-f=\"knee|knees\" data-n=\"3\">1–2 knees</span>",
     "name_html": "Pork knee / knuckle (trotters)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "enough to fill the pot about halfway",
     "name_html": "Chicken bones (drumstick bones, backs)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "about as much as the chicken",
     "name_html": "Beef neck bones"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Rinse the bones under cold water and scrub off dark bits, clotted blood and scum (the beef neck bones have the most).</li><li>This is what keeps the finished broth white rather than grey.</li><li>Keep the pork and beef bones in the fridge until their stage.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Scrub and rinse",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Scrub every bone under cold running water — dark bits, blood and scum off.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/3-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/3.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": "Broth",
   "part_id": "part-broth",
   "time": "~15 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~15 min</span>",
   "title": "Scrub and rinse",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Into the dashi:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>chicken bones</li><li>onion <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-n=\"1\">1</span></span></li></ul></li><li>Bring it up on <b>medium heat</b>, then turn it <b>low</b> and let it simmer, lid ajar.</li><li>Top up with boiling water whenever the bones start to poke out; scrape the bottom now and then so nothing catches.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium, then low",
    "label_html": "<span>medium, then low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Stage 1 — chicken + onion, 6–8 hours",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Chicken bones and onion go into the dashi first.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/4-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Keep it at a low simmer; top up with boiling water when the bones poke out.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/4-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/4.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": "Broth",
   "part_id": "part-broth",
   "time": "6–8 h",
   "time_html": "<span>6–8 h</span>",
   "title": "Stage 1 — chicken + onion, 6–8 hours",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "enough to fill the pot about halfway",
     "name_html": "Chicken bones (drumstick bones, backs)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "as needed",
     "name_html": "Boiling water for topping up"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lift the chicken bones and onion out with the spider strainer — the broth stays in the pot.</li><li>Add:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>pork knee / knuckle (trotters) <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-f=\"knee|knees\" data-n=\"3\">1–2 knees</span></span></li><li>ginger for the broth <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"30\">30 g</span></span></li><li>garlic head <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-n=\"1\">1</span></span></li></ul></li><li>Back up on medium, then low again, topping up as before. The broth turns cloudy and richer.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium, then low",
    "label_html": "<span>medium, then low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-5",
