  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Mix until the sugar dissolves:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>soy sauce <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"200\">200 ml</span></span></li><li>mirin <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"100\">100 ml</span></span></li><li>sake <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"100\">100 ml</span></span></li><li>brown sugar <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"60\">60 g</span></span></li><li>water <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"200\">200 ml</span></span></li></ul></li><li>Add:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>garlic <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"4\" data-f=\"clove|cloves\" data-n=\"1\">4 cloves</span></span></li><li>ginger <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"20\">20 g</span></span></li><li>spring onion greens <span class=\"amt\">a handful</span></li></ul></li><li>Roll the belly up tightly from a long side, <b>skin side out</b>, and tie it with kitchen string every ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 cm</span>.</li><li>Put the roll in a snug dish, turn it in the marinade and leave it in the fridge for <b>about 12 hours</b>, turning a few times.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-8",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Roll, tie and marinate the belly",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Stir the marinade until the sugar is gone.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/8-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Roll the belly up tightly from a long side, skin side out, and tie it with string every 2 cm.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/8-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/8.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 8,
   "part": "Chashu",
   "part_id": "part-chashu",
   "time": "~12 h",
   "time_html": "<span>~12 h</span>",
   "title": "Roll, tie and marinate the belly",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"kg\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"1.2\">1–1.2 kg</span>",
     "name_html": "Pork belly"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Seam side down in the dish with its marinade, uncovered, into a very hot oven.</li><li>After 30 minutes, baste it with the juices and give it another 30 minutes, until the outside is deeply browned.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "oven 230 °C",
    "label_html": "<span>oven <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"230\" data-s=\"0\">230 °C</span></span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-9",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Roast hot",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "After 30 minutes, baste it with the juices, then 30 more.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/9-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/9.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 9,
   "part": "Chashu",
   "part_id": "part-chashu",
   "time": "~1 h",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 h</span>",
   "title": "Roast hot",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Turn the oven down and keep roasting, basting now and then, until a skewer slides into the middle of the roll with no resistance.</p>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "oven 120 °C",
    "label_html": "<span>oven <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"120\" data-s=\"0\">120 °C</span></span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-10",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Then low until tender",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/ramen/10.webp",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 10,
   "part": "Chashu",
   "part_id": "part-chashu",
   "time": "1–1½ h",
   "time_html": "<span>1–1½ h</span>",
   "title": "Then low until tender",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lift the roll out (keep the liquid for tare).</li><li>Let it cool, then wrap it and refrigerate — overnight is best — until it’s cold and firm.</li><li>Firm pork slices cleanly.</li><li>Cut and pull off the string, then slice into rounds about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 mm</span> thick while it’s still cold.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-11",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Chill until firm, untie, slice",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Cold from the fridge: cut and pull off the string.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/11-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Slice into 5 mm rounds, fingertips tucked.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/11-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/11.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 11,
   "part": "Chashu",
   "part_id": "part-chashu",
   "time": "chill overnight",
   "time_html": "<span>chill overnight</span>",
   "title": "Chill until firm, untie, slice",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li><i>Suggestion — your notes don’t mention a tare.</i></li><li>Strain the cooking liquid, skim the fat off (keep it: a spoon on top of the bowl is great) and simmer to reduce by about a third.</li><li>Taste: it should be very salty and sweet on its own — it seasons the plain broth.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-12",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Reduce the marinade into tare",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Skim the fat off the strained liquid, then reduce by a third.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/12-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/12.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 12,
   "part": "Tare",
   "part_id": "part-tare",
   "time": "~20 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~20 min</span>",
   "title": "Reduce the marinade into tare",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"250\">250 ml</span>",
     "name_html": "Chashu marinade, strained and reduced"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Rinse the tentacles (if raw, rub with salt and rinse to remove slime).</li><li>Seal each whole tentacle in its own vacuum or zip bag, air pressed out, and cook it in the water bath at around <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"77\" data-s=\"0\">77 °C</span> for about 5 h</b>.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "water bath 77 °C",
    "label_html": "<span>water bath <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"77\" data-s=\"0\">77 °C</span></span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-13",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Sous vide the tentacle",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Raw tentacles: rub with salt, then rinse the slime off.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/13-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Seal each tentacle in its own bag and lower it into the 77 °C bath.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/13-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/13.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 13,
   "part": "Octopus",
   "part_id": "part-octopus",
   "time": "~5 h",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 h</span>",
   "title": "Sous vide the tentacle",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "1 per bowl",
     "name_html": "Octopus tentacles (large octopus)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lift the tentacles out of the bags and pat them dry.</li><li>Keep each tentacle <b>whole</b> — no slicing; it goes on the bowl in one piece.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-14",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Pat dry — keep it whole",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Pat dry and keep it whole — it goes on the bowl in one piece.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/14-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/14.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 14,
   "part": "Octopus",
   "part_id": "part-octopus",
   "time": "~10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~10 min</span>",
   "title": "Pat dry — keep it whole",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Right before serving, sear the chashu slices in a very hot dry pan for 30–60 seconds a side (or hit them with a torch) until caramelised at the edges.</li><li>Sear each whole tentacle in a hot pan with a little oil, then add a splash of soy sauce and turn it until it’s glazed and charred at the edges.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "high",
    "label_html": "<span>high</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-15",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Sear chashu; sear the octopus with soy",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Sear the tentacle in a little oil, then add a splash of soy and turn until glazed and charred.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/15-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/15.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 15,
   "part": "Noodles & assembly",
   "part_id": "part-noodles--assembly",
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Sear chashu; sear the octopus with soy",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "2–3 slices",
     "name_html": "Chashu"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "1 whole tentacle",
     "name_html": "Octopus"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "a little",
     "name_html": "Oil for searing the octopus"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "a splash",
     "name_html": "Soy sauce for searing the octopus"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Fill the bowls with boiling water while everything else comes together; tip it out just before building.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-16",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Warm the bowls",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Fill the bowls with boiling water; tip it out just before building.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/16-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/16.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 16,
   "part": "Noodles & assembly",
   "part_id": "part-noodles--assembly",
   "time": "2 min",
   "time_html": "<span>2 min</span>",
   "title": "Warm the bowls",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>2–3 tablespoons of tare into each bowl, then <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"350\" data-s=\"0\">350 ml</span> of <b>boiling</b> broth.</li><li>Whisk briefly to blend and froth it.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-17",
