    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cook the fresh alkaline noodles (homemade: <a href=\"alkaline-ramen-noodles.html\">alkaline ramen noodles</a>, made with baked baking soda) in a big pot of boiling unsalted water — thin fresh noodles usually take 1–2 min.</li><li>Drain hard — any water dilutes the broth.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "high",
    "label_html": "<span>high</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-18",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Cook the noodles",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Drain hard — shake out every drop of water.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/18-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/18.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 18,
   "part": "Noodles & assembly",
   "part_id": "part-noodles--assembly",
   "time": "1–2 min",
   "time_html": "<span>1–2 min</span>",
   "title": "Cook the noodles",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"120\" data-b=\"140\" data-s=\"0\">120–140 g</span> — homemade: <a href=\"alkaline-ramen-noodles.html\">alkaline ramen noodles</a> (baked baking soda)",
     "name_html": "Fresh alkaline ramen noodles (thin)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Fold the noodles into the broth.</li><li>Top with:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>chashu <span class=\"amt\">2–3 slices</span></li><li>octopus <span class=\"amt\">1 whole tentacle</span></li><li>spring onion <span class=\"amt\">sliced</span></li><li>nori <span class=\"amt\">1 piece</span></li><li>toasted sesame <span class=\"amt\">a pinch</span></li><li>soft-boiled egg (<a href=\"ramen-egg.html\">6-minute</a>), halved</li></ul></li><li>The tentacle goes on whole, in one piece. Eat straight away.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-19",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Top and serve",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Fold the noodles into the broth, then lay the toppings on.",
      "src": "illustrations/ramen/19-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/ramen/19.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 19,
   "part": "Noodles & assembly",
   "part_id": "part-noodles--assembly",
   "time": null,
   "time_html": null,
   "title": "Top and serve",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "½, optional — <a href=\"ramen-egg.html\">6-minute egg</a>",
     "name_html": "Soft-boiled egg"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Chashu:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>vacuum-seal the slices one by one, so you can take out exactly what you need</li></ul></li><li>Octopus:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>vacuum-seal the tentacles, still whole</li></ul></li><li>Broth:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>strain it through cheesecloth</li><li>cool it, then refrigerate for a night (~24 h) until it sets into a jelly</li><li>spoon or cut the jelly into silicone molds and freeze it into large cubes</li><li>pop the cubes out and wrap each one in aluminium foil — they store very well</li></ul></li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-20",
